    {
      "identifier": "nickel_campbell_2009_bm3_mgd",
      "label": "Campbell et al. (2009), fcc Ni, 295 K BM3-Debye",
      "model": "BM3",
      "temperature_ref": 295.0,
      "parameters": {
        "V0": {"value": 43.751883341896516, "error": null, "fixed": true},
        "K0": {"value": 179.0, "error": 3},
        "K0_prime": {"value": 4.3, "error": 0.2}
      },
      "thermal": {
        "model": "MieGruneisenDebye",
        "parameters": {
          "Tr": {"value": 295.0, "error": null, "fixed": true},
          "theta0": {"value": 415.0, "error": null, "fixed": true},
          "gamma0": {"value": 2.5, "error": 0.06},
          "n": {"value": 1.0, "error": null, "fixed": true},
          "q": {"value": 1.0, "error": null, "fixed": true}
        },
        "debye_temperature_law": "variable_exponent"
      },
      "parameter_error_confidence": null,
      "experimental_pressure_range_gpa": [2.336174779961698, 65.9],
      "experimental_temperature_range_k": [298.0, 2457.07],
      "determination_method": "experimental",
      "notes": "Equation (5) and Table 1: 295 K BM3 plus Mie-Gruneisen-Debye, gamma=gamma0*(V/V0)^q and theta=theta0*(V/V0)^(-gamma(V)). No explicit electronic or anharmonic pressure. Source molar V0 is converted to the Z=4 conventional cell using exact SI Avogadro constant. Italicized Table 1 values are held fixed, and nonitalic values with errors are fitted. The confidence convention and covariance of published errors are not specified. Temperature-corrected workbook values are used as printed; no second correction is applied. All 101 source rows are bundled. Nine quenched DAC states are retained but excluded from the main 92-row refit because Section 2.2 warns of residual stresses; an all-row sensitivity fit is reported. ",
      "range_provenance": {
        "source_location": "Tables S2-S3; Seagle (2008) Table 1 and subsolidus supplement for Fe/FeO",
        "notes": "Marginal experimental coverage, not a rectangular phase-stability field. Fe/FeO upper bounds include earlier Seagle approximate isobars; new-study-only bounds and selected-row extrema are in the reproduction JSON. fcc Fe and stoichiometric B1 FeO must remain within their source phase/composition fields. The 295 K reference is an extrapolation. NiO is a source cubic-average B1 model across unresolved magnetic distortion."
      },
      "fit_datasets": ["ni_nio_campbell_2009_table_s3_pvt"],
      "reference": {
        "authors": ["Campbell", "Danielson", "Righter", "Seagle", "Wang", "Prakapenka"],
        "year": 2009,
        "title": "High pressure effects on the iron–iron oxide and nickel–nickel oxide oxygen fugacity buffers",
        "source": "Earth and Planetary Science Letters",
        "volume": "286",
        "locator": "556-564",
        "doi": "10.1016/j.epsl.2009.07.022"
      },
      "pressure_calibration": {
        "status": "resolved",
        "audit_date": "2026-09-19",
        "methods": [
          {
            "kind": "equation_of_state",
            "material": "NaCl B1",
            "reference": {
              "authors": ["Decker"],
              "year": 1971,
              "source": "Journal of Applied Physics",
              "volume": "42",
              "locator": "3239-3244",
              "doi": "10.1063/1.1660714"
            },
            "source_location": "Sections 2.1-2.2; Tables S2-S3, NaCl B1 rows"
          },
          {
            "kind": "equation_of_state",
            "material": "NaCl B2",
            "reference": {
              "authors": ["Fei", "Ricolleau", "Frank", "Mibe", "Shen", "Prakapenka"],
              "year": 2007,
              "source": "PNAS",
              "volume": "104",
              "locator": "9182-9186",
              "doi": "10.1073/pnas.0609013104"
            },
            "source_location": "Section 2.2; Tables S2-S3, NaCl B2 rows"
          }
        ],
        "recalculation": {
          "status": "reference_eos_not_bundled",
          "notes": "Paired NaCl phase, molar volume, effective temperature and their errors are bundled for every current-study row. The exact Decker B1/Fei B2 pair is not registered as a complete executable catalog calibration route. Use the tabulated pressure; do not substitute a newer NaCl scale. Seagle fit-input rows have Fe volumes and temperatures but no NaCl readings or individual pressures."
        },
        "notes": "MAP detector angle calibrated with NaCl a=5.6402 A (JCPDS 05-0628); DAC geometry with CeO2. MAP cooling cycles minimize deviatoric stress. The article writes DAC T_sample=295+0.97*(T_meas-295) and T_NaCl=(3*T_meas+295)/4. The workbook uses a 293 K baseline for some Ni-NiO DAC runs and 295 K for others; preserve its stored values. Equation (4) prints sigma_TNaCl=(T_meas-295)/2, while the hot DAC workbook rows use (T_meas-T_ambient)/4; preserve the workbook uncertainties. The workbook pressure-threshold footnote is approximate: honor the explicit NaCl phase column, including B2 rows below 26 GPa."
      },
